.TH TOWER-TRAY 1 "" "tower @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tower\-tray \- Tower's radar in the top bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tower-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tower-tray
puts Tower's radar in your top bar and a panel behind it: guard status, network
weather, every running Claude Code agent, your location, keep-awake, and plan
usage. It is the Linux counterpart of Tower's macOS menu-bar app.
.PP
It starts
.BR towerd (1)
if it is not already running, so this one command arms the guard and shows it.
Like every Tower front-end it is thin: it reads
.I ~/.tower/state.json
and writes command files into
.IR ~/.tower/cmd/ .
.SH THE MARK IS THE STATE
The radar has five looks, one per guard state: a calm pulse with live blips
while guarding, a rotating sweep while confirming your location, an amber
dashed ring with sonar pings when there is no usable path to Anthropic, an
amber ring with a fence and a lunging blip when you are off-country, and a red
dashed ring with a hollow core when routing is off and Claude is unguarded.
Amber means *held* — pending, and it clears itself; red means unguarded.
.PP
While keep-awake is on, the radar's core lights as a neutral lamp; the
lid-closed vigil breathes. It is never amber or red, so a guard hold always
outranks it.
.PP
Motion is information: a hold or a sweep animates, a clear guard with nothing
running is completely still, and the desktop's own "reduce animations" setting
freezes every state at a legible still frame.
.SH USING IT
Left-click the radar for the menu — status, the guard toggle, keep-awake,
target country, the running agents, and
.BR "Open Tower…" ,
which opens the full panel. Middle-click opens the panel directly. Closing the
panel never stops the guard.
.SH DANGEROUS ACTIONS
Turning the guard off and quitting Tower both let Claude reach the API
unguarded, so each is warned and confirmed twice. The warning says how many
agents are working right now, and quitting also says how many chats are pinned
to the proxy and will lose their connection until restarted.
.SH AT LOGIN
.RS
.B systemctl --user enable --now tower-tray.service
.RE
.PP
Or copy
.I /usr/share/applications/tower-tray.desktop
into
.IR ~/.config/autostart .
.SH GNOME
The top bar shows a StatusNotifierItem only through the shipped appindicator
extension. Ubuntu's GNOME session enables it by default; elsewhere:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo apt install gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
.br
.B gnome-extensions enable ubuntu-appindicators@ubuntu.com
.RE
.PP
KDE, XFCE, Cinnamon and Budgie need nothing extra.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/tower/icons
rendered radar frames (a cache; safe to delete)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tower (1),
.BR towerd (1)
